=== (stage 2) superadditivity vs DRIVE AMPLITUDE ===
# superadditivity at amp 1.0 reports the drive size, not the sheet: the
# sigmoid curvature scale is slope = 4 mV and a 0.1 mV perturbation gives a
# second-order term of (0.1/4)^2 = 6e-4.  so sweep the amplitude.
amp=1 base  transport 9.561e-06  superadd 1.0002
amp=1 aniso  transport 9.843e-03  superadd 1.0014
